+## Submission tools in Routing
+
+A tool may opt into native routing history with
+`magpie: {route: {provider, modelArg?, defaultModel}}`. The host validates
+and exposes this optional metadata on `plugin.Tool.Route`; ordinary tools
+remain unchanged. `runRoutedPluginTool` records one tool execution in the
+same gateway trace and recent-call ring as other requests. Direct plugin
+MCP, the per-plugin endpoint and the Library hub all reach it; caller key,
+agent and explicit session headers are retained. It neither retries nor
+submits a second generation. Poll/status/download tools opt out.
+
+For asynchronous video submissions, HTTP 200 means the submitting tool
+returned, not that video generation finished. Recent-call response details
+contain only operation, job ID, reported job status, account ID and an
+explicit generation-completed flag. The durable route stores the returned
+job ID as responseId. No prompt, media bytes, frame path or arbitrary tool
+output is copied into these details, and no token or monetary charge is
+inferred. Generation progress remains available through the plugin's status
+tool. Old tool calls made before this integration have no routing record.
+
+Tests: `TestPluginVideoSubmissionRoutes`,
+`TestPluginVideoSubmissionRoutesThroughHub`,
+`TestPluginVideoRouteCallerAndCanceled`, and `TestPluginTools`.
